- $\\lambda Δx=3.2$\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the RK4 method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δ)=1-\\lambda Δx+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{4}}{24}.\n$$" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328723 1113 #uuid "ff08560f-20d2-5d31-aa35-62c5ff460f0e" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328723 1145 "A numerical method\n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the RK4 Method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(\\lambda Δx)^{4}}{24}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the RK4 Method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.5)| & =|1-0.5+\\frac{(0.5)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(0.5)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(0.5)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{233}{384}| \\\\  & =0.606…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the RK4 Method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.5)| & =|1-1.5+\\frac{(1.5)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(1.5)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(1.5)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{35}{128}| \\\\  & =0.273…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the RK4 Method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=2.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(2.5)| & =|1-2.5+\\frac{(2.5)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(2.5)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(2.5)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{83}{128}| \\\\  & =0.648…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the RK4 Method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=3.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(3)| & =|1-3.2+\\frac{(3.2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(3.2)^{3}}{6}+\\frac{(3.2)^{4}}{24}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{3427}{1875}| \\\\  & =1.827…<1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *outside* the stability region, the RK4 Method is unstable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only\".\n\nNote that the stability region of the RK4 Method is $0<\\lambda Δx<2.785…,$ so it is not absolutely stable." 13194139535053 true] [17592186328724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328725 13194139535053 true] [17592186328724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328726 13194139535053 true] [17592186328724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328727 13194139535053 true] [17592186328724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328728 13194139535053 true] [17592186328724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328729 13194139535053 true] [17592186328724 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535053 true] [17592186328724 1041 "selection" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328724 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328728 13194139535053 true] [17592186328724 1110 #uuid "89aee0a3-adac-53e2-9e48-14003b60a0cf" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328725 1034 "I only" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535053 true] [17592186328725 1111 #uuid "24c83297-9b40-5ea1-94ca-47a631d30637" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328726 1034 "None" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535053 true] [17592186328726 1111 #uuid "fb5aee17-d3b1-59d9-aa84-2b92d9a513dc" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328727 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535053 true] [17592186328727 1111 #uuid "8c60976a-df5e-56cb-abfd-6832b1981248" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328728 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139535053 true] [17592186328728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535053 true] [17592186328728 1111 #uuid "fc55921